Scenario
You are building a Spring Boot REST API called Secure User Registry API that handles user registration and authentication.
Each User has:
• id (auto-generated)
• username (unique, 5–20 characters, alphanumeric + underscore only)
• password (hashed with BCrypt before storage — never stored as plain text)
• fullName (max 100 characters)
• age (between 0 and 120)
API clients (via Postman) can:
• Register a new user at POST /auth/signup — public (no authentication required)
• List all users at GET /users — protected (authentication required; response must NOT expose passwords)
• Get their own profile at GET /auth/me — protected
• Check the service is alive at GET /health — public
Data is stored in a PostgreSQL database.

